# GitHub Personal Access Token (classic or fine-grained)
# Permissions needed: Read-only access to public repositories
#
# How to create one:
# 1. Go to https://github.com/settings/tokens/new
# 2. Give it a name (e.g. "portfolio-api")
# 3. Set expiration (e.g. 1 year)
# 4. Check "public_repo" under repo scope  (or no scopes for public-only)
# 5. Click "Generate token" and copy it here
#
# For Vercel deployment:
# - Go to your Vercel project → Settings → Environment Variables
# - Add GITHUB_TOKEN with your token value
# - Redeploy for it to take effect
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_token_here
